course: dictionary
lesson: 10242
title: Tolerant: accepting and patient
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tolerant is an adjective, so it describes a person, a plant or a way of behaving. Its main meaning is accepting and respecting other people's beliefs, ways of life or opinions, even when they are different from yours.
explain: «The Persian Empire was well organised and fairly tolerant for its time.» Here tolerant describes how a whole empire treated people with different beliefs and ways of life. Check your meaning by swapping in "accepting of different people": the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Tolerant can also mean patient with things that might annoy you, or able to survive hard conditions, like a drought-tolerant plant. The words around it show which meaning is correct, so always read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Tolerant means accepting and respecting people whose beliefs, ways of life or opinions are different from yours.
fact: «Tolerant» can also mean patient with things that annoy you.
fact: In science, «drought-tolerant» means a plant can survive with very little water.
fact: «Intolerant» is the opposite: «lactose intolerant» people get ill from milk.
fact: Tolerant is an adjective, so it has forms like more tolerant and most tolerant.
exercise: «The Persian Empire was well organised and fairly tolerant for its time.» What does tolerant mean here? | *Accepting of people with different beliefs and ways of life | Angry with anyone who was different | Very small in size | Able to stay under water for hours
exercise: Mia's garden is full of drought-tolerant plants. What does drought-tolerant mean? | *Able to survive with very little water | Able to grow in the rain every day | Fond of a cup of tea | Very tall and thin
exercise: Sam waited calmly while his little brother spilled the paint again. Which word fits best to describe Sam? | treacherous | ancient | *tolerant | famished
test: Ruby stayed calm when the bus was late again. Which word describes her best? | Famished | Glum | Ancient | *Tolerant
test: «Lactose intolerant» means what? | Able to survive a drought | *Unable to take milk without becoming ill | Patient with noise | Fond of other cultures
exam: Which meaning fits in «The club is tolerant of every religion and culture»? | *Accepting and respecting people who are different from you | Able to survive in harsh places | Very old | Patient with noise
